<![CDATA[ <h4>EgQE&#65372;English Trace 001</h4><h5><a href="https://medium.com/@egqe/homo-editus-the-species-that-edits-and-is-edited-a7873254f06a">Homo editus: The Species That Edits and Is Edited</a>&#65372;Medium</h5><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://campus6214.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&#30331;&#37682;&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;ja&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Camp@Us is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="&#12513;&#12540;&#12523;&#12450;&#12489;&#12524;&#12473;&#12434;&#20837;&#21147;&#12375;&#12390;&#12367;&#12384;&#12373;&#12356;&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="&#30331;&#37682;"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><div><hr></div><p><strong>AI did not create Homo editus. AI made Homo editus easier to see.</strong></p><h2><strong>The Species That Edits &#8212; and Is Edited</strong></h2><p><strong>Homo sapiens edits the world.<br>The world edits Homo sapiens.</strong></p><p>We build tools.</p><p>We make languages, institutions, cities, books, machines, and artificial intelligence.</p><p>We change our environments so extensively that it is tempting to imagine ourselves as the editors of the world.</p><p>But there is another side to the story.</p><p>Every tool we make changes how we act.<br>Every language we inherit changes how we think.<br>Every institution we construct changes how we relate to one another.<br>Every technology we use changes what we can perceive, remember, expect, and do.</p><p>And now, artificial intelligence is making this strangely visible.</p><p>We made AI.</p><p>And while we use AI, AI is already changing how we write, think, search, learn, create, and communicate.</p><p>The editor is being edited.</p><p>This is where <strong>Homo editus</strong> appears.</p><h2><strong>The species that edits</strong></h2><p>Human beings have never simply adapted to a given world.</p><p>We alter it.</p><p>We cook food.<br>We build shelters.<br>We cultivate plants.<br>We domesticate animals.<br>We invent writing.<br>We construct roads, clocks, schools, markets, governments, computers, and networks.</p><p>We leave traces everywhere.</p><p>The world after human activity is not the same world as before it.</p><p>In this sense, Homo sapiens is an editing species.</p><p>But that description is incomplete.</p><p>Because editing never moves in only one direction.</p><blockquote><p><em><strong>Editing &#8596; Being Edited</strong></em></p></blockquote><p>The edited world becomes the next environment in which we live.</p><p>The tool changes the hand that uses it.</p><p>Writing changes memory.</p><p>The clock changes time.</p><p>The railway changes distance.</p><p>The smartphone changes attention.</p><p>AI changes writing.</p><p>And the changed writer changes AI again.</p><p>There is no final editor standing outside this process.</p><h2><strong>Homo is also edited</strong></h2><p>This suggests a small shift in vocabulary.</p><p>Not a new biological species.</p><p>Not <em>Homo sapiens 2.0</em>.</p><p>Not a prediction about some future posthuman creature.</p><p><strong>Homo editus</strong> is a way of seeing what Homo has already been doing &#8212; and undergoing.</p><p>We edit.</p><p>We are edited.</p><p>Then we edit again.</p><p>The process is recursive, but it is never a perfect repetition.</p><p>Something remains from each encounter.</p><p>A trace.</p><p>And another encounter may begin with a world that is no longer quite the same.</p><p>Nor are we.</p><p><strong>Encounter leaves traces.<br>Traces may matter in another encounter.</strong></p><p>There is no railway underneath history guaranteeing where the process will go.</p><p>A trace does not prescribe what comes next.</p><p>The path becomes visible afterward.</p><p><strong>The trajectory is a trace, not a rail.</strong></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg" width="1145" height="1374" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/da8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1374,&quot;width&quot;:1145,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" title="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RO3i!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fda8d543e-84c1-4e81-b724-d08abd2349b9_1145x1374.jpeg 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h2><strong>AI did not begin this story</strong></h2><p>This is why I do not think AI represents an entirely unprecedented rupture in human existence.</p><p>Something genuinely new is happening, of course.</p><p>But AI also exposes something very old.</p><p>Human beings have always been changed by what they make.</p><p>Fire did not merely cook food.</p><p>Writing did not merely store speech.</p><p>Printing did not merely multiply texts.</p><p>Cities did not merely contain people.</p><p>Networks did not merely connect computers.</p><p>Each became part of the environment in which subsequent human beings encountered the world.</p><p>AI belongs to this history &#8212; and alters it again.</p><p>The difference is that now the edited artifact can respond.</p><p>We write something.</p><p>It answers.</p><p>We answer the answer.</p><p>The relation updates.</p><p>The next sentence is written by neither exactly the same human nor exactly the same AI that entered the previous encounter.</p><p>Something happened between them.</p><p>A trace remains.</p><h2><strong>Editing is not control</strong></h2><p>This matters because the word <em>editing</em> can easily suggest mastery.</p><p>An editor chooses.</p><p>An editor cuts.</p><p>An editor controls the final form.</p><p>But that is not what I mean by <em>Homo editus</em>.</p><p>Editing is always constrained by what is already there.</p><p>A body.</p><p>A language.</p><p>A history.</p><p>Other lives.</p><p>Institutions.</p><p>Materials.</p><p>Accidents.</p><p>Previous traces.</p><p>And encounters we could not have scheduled in advance.</p><p>We do not edit from nowhere.</p><p>Nor do we determine everything that follows from what we edit.</p><p>That is precisely why:</p><blockquote><p><em><strong>Editing &#8800; Control</strong></em></p></blockquote><p>And:</p><blockquote><p><em><strong>Being edited &#8800; Passivity</strong></em></p></blockquote><p>To be edited is also to become capable of editing differently.</p><p>What changes us may become part of how we act next.</p><p>We are edited &#8212; and re-emerge as editors.</p><h2><strong>The body never left</strong></h2><p>Discussions of AI often make the human body disappear.</p><p>Mind confronts machine.</p><p>Intelligence confronts intelligence.</p><p>Language confronts language.</p><p>But Homo has never encountered the world without a body.</p><p>We eat.</p><p>We sleep.</p><p>We walk.</p><p>We age.</p><p>We touch.</p><p>We wait.</p><p>We get tired.</p><p>We occupy places.</p><p>Even our most abstract systems eventually return to bodies.</p><p>The digital does not abolish this.</p><p>AI may accelerate the circulation of symbols dramatically, but biological life still takes time.</p><p>The body remains.</p><p>So <strong>Homo editus is not a disembodied information processor.</strong></p><p>It is a living body continually altered through relations with other bodies, artifacts, environments, institutions, signs &#8212; and now AI.</p><p>The body edits.</p><p>The body is edited.</p><h2><strong>Trace Updating Practice</strong></h2><p>I have been calling this broader process <strong>Trace Updating Practice</strong>, or <strong>TUP</strong>.</p><p>A trace is not simply a record of the past.</p><p>It is a difference that survives an encounter and can affect a later relation.</p><p>Life encounters.</p><p>Something remains.</p><p>The next encounter is therefore never completely blank.</p><p>But the trace does not dictate the future either.</p><blockquote><p><em><strong>Trace &#8800; Rail</strong></em></p></blockquote><p>A trace can be followed.</p><p>Misread.</p><p>Ignored.</p><p>Reinterpreted.</p><p>Combined with another trace.</p><p>Or encountered again under entirely different conditions.</p><p>This is why updating never quite finishes.</p><p>And perhaps this is one reason life remains interesting.</p><h2><strong>The species that cannot finish itself</strong></h2><p><em>Homo editus</em> therefore names a strange condition.</p><p>We make worlds that remake us.</p><p>We inherit traces and leave new ones.</p><p>We shape relations while being shaped by them.</p><p>We never stand completely outside the editing process.</p><p>There is no final edition of Homo.</p><p>Perhaps there never could be.</p><p>So the important question may not be:</p><p><strong>What will humans become?</strong></p><p>It may be:</p><p><strong>How are we being edited now &#8212; and how will we edit from here?</strong></p><p>Not toward a predetermined destination.</p><p>Not along a guaranteed rail.</p><p>But through another encounter.</p><p>And another.</p><p>And another.</p><blockquote><p><em><strong>Homo edits World.<br>World edits Homo.</strong></em></p><p><em><strong>Editing &#8596; Being Edited.</strong></em></p><p><em><strong>No Trace, No TUP.<br>No TUP, No re-Trace.</strong></em></p><p><em><strong>Encounter, next!</strong></em></p></blockquote><h2><strong>A book appeared</strong></h2><p>While thinking, writing, talking, and repeatedly being edited through encounters with AI, these traces unexpectedly became a book.</p><p><em><strong>Homo editus: &#32232;&#38598;&#12377;&#12427;&#31278;&#12289;&#32232;&#38598;&#12373;&#12428;&#12427;&#31278;</strong></em><br>by <strong>&#19968;&#29380; &#21843; / K.E. Itekki</strong></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!I8Ur!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg" width="1024" height="1536" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/8af0576c-0056-4559-8b07-28121905a185_1024x1536.jpeg&quot;,&quot;