HYLLBBR?linkCode=ll2&amp;tag=hatenadia0516-22&amp;linkId=8752d76391c3f76e207089910da7d330&amp;ref_=as_li_ss_tl">Homo editus: &#32232;&#38598;&#12377;&#12427;&#31278;&#12289;&#32232;&#38598;&#12373;&#12428;&#12427;&#31278;</a></strong></em><strong> by &#19968;&#29380; &#21843; / K.E. Itekki</strong></p><p><strong>More tunnels are already being dug.</strong></p><p>I publish ongoing essays and research notes on <strong><a href="https://note.com/takahashihajime">note</a></strong>, exploring <em>Homo editus</em>, Trace Updating Practice (TUP), AI, life, language, institutions, and whatever I encounter next.</p><p>The original essays are written mainly in Japanese and can also be read through note&#8217;s automatic translation into English and Korean.</p><p>Translation is not a copy.<br>It is another encounter.</p><p><strong>Translation &#8800; Copy.<br>Translation is re-Encounter.</strong></p><p>Read. Trace. Misread. Translate. ZURE.<br>And perhaps, encounter again.</p><p><strong>Trace without Rail.<br>Encounter, next!</strong></p><div><hr></div><p><strong><a href="https://medium.com/@egqe/homo-editus-the-species-that-edits-and-is-edited-a7873254f06a">I&#65372;Species</a></strong><a href="https://medium.com/@egqe/homo-editus-the-species-that-edits-and-is-edited-a7873254f06a"><br></a><em>What is Homo editus?</em></p><p><strong><a href="https://medium.com/@egqe/ai-did-not-invent-homo-editus-it-made-the-editing-visible-2f4fabdeee3a">II&#65372;Relation</a></strong><br><em>What becomes visible when AI enters the encounter?</em></p><p><strong><a href="https://medium.com/@egqe/the-editor-is-one-of-the-outputs-of-editing-737bf7424692">III&#65372;Subject</a></strong><br><em>What happens to the editor through editing?</em></p><p></p> ]]>
