M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><h3>&#24466;&#28982;&#12395;&#12394;&#12382;&#12426;&#12390;&#35598;&#12427;&#30701;&#27468;&#12363;&#12394;</h3><blockquote><h4>005 &#8212; Tracing into Mystery</h4></blockquote><div><hr></div><div class="callout-block" data-callout="true"><h4>Inter-Phase Co-Editing</h4><p><em>A poem is not translated. It continues becoming across phases.</em><br><em>Rewritten across languages, intelligences, and time.</em></p><p><strong>Un po&#232;me ne se traduit pas. Il continue de devenir &#224; travers les phases.</strong><br><em>R&#233;&#233;crit &#224; travers les langues, les intelligences et le temps.</em></p></div><div><hr></div><h3>01</h3><p><strong>&#24466;&#28982;&#12395;&#12394;&#12382;&#12426;&#12390;&#35598;&#12427;&#30701;&#27468;&#12363;&#12394;<br>&#29356;&#12395;&#24341;&#12363;&#12428;&#12390;&#22823;&#36335;&#12418;&#36066;&#12418;</strong></p><p>Idly tracing, I wander into mystery&#8212;<br>a tanka, perhaps,<br>led by a dog,<br>along the great road,<br>tracing even the wise.</p><p>&#192; loisir, je trace et j&#8217;entre dans l&#8217;&#233;nigme &#8212;<br>un tanka, peut-&#234;tre,<br>tir&#233; par un chien,<br>sur la grande route,<br>jusqu&#8217;&#224; suivre m&#234;me les sages.</p><div><hr></div><h3>02</h3><p><strong>&#25945;&#31034;&#12394;&#12367;&#22823;&#36335;&#12434;&#36208;&#12425;&#12400;&#20449;&#22833;&#12379;&#12390;<br>&#22467;&#12414;&#12415;&#12428;&#12398;&#30684;&#25345;&#12395;&#35463;&#12426;</strong></p><p>Run the great road without guidance,<br>and trust falls away&#8212;<br>pride takes pride<br>in its own dignity,<br>covered in dust.</p><p>Courir la grande route sans guide,<br>et la confiance se perd &#8212;<br>la fiert&#233; s&#8217;enorgueillit<br>de sa propre dignit&#233;,<br>couverte de poussi&#232;re.</p><div><hr></div><h3>03</h3><p><strong>&#28961;&#37969;&#23450;&#37202;&#12394;&#12425;&#32654;&#21619;&#12356;&#12364;&#34892;&#31243;&#12398;<br>&#38560;&#12428;&#12435;&#25151;&#12399;&#36991;&#12369;&#12394;&#12365;&#12419;&#19981;&#21619;&#12356;</strong></p><p>Unjudged wine may taste just fine,<br>but when the making<br>hides in a secret room,<br>better stay away&#8212;<br>or the taste turns bitter.</p><p>Un vin sans expertise peut &#234;tre d&#233;licieux,<br>mais si sa fabrication<br>se cache dans une chambre secr&#232;te,<br>mieux vaut s&#8217;en d&#233;tourner &#8212;<br>sinon le go&#251;t tourne mal.</p><div><hr></div><h3>04</h3><p><strong>&#23455;&#12427;&#12411;&#12393;&#39449;&#12426;&#12390;&#22549;&#12388;&#12427;&#31179;&#12388;&#12427;&#12409;<br>&#24115;&#23611;&#12354;&#12431;&#12379;&#12398;&#19981;&#23455;&#12418;&#29087;&#12375;</strong></p><p>The fuller the fruit, the richer the deceit&#8212;<br>autumn drops like a well bucket;<br>even dishonesty ripens,<br>settling accounts<br>before it falls.</p><p>Plus le fruit m&#251;rit, plus le mensonge s&#8217;&#233;paissit &#8212;<br>l&#8217;automne tombe comme un seau au puits ;<br>m&#234;me la d&#233;loyaut&#233; m&#251;rit,<br>ajustant ses comptes<br>avant la chute.</p><div><hr></div><h3>05</h3><p><strong>&#12431;&#12428;&#12418;&#12377;&#12360;&#12456;&#12473;&#12456;&#12492;&#12456;&#12473;&#12398;&#12383;&#12381;&#12363;&#12428;&#12395;<br>&#29305;&#12395;&#38598;&#12417;&#12390;&#12394;&#12395;&#12363;&#12383;&#12425;&#12435;&#12420;</strong></p><p>My own days decline;<br>social media too enters twilight.<br>Why gather anything<br>especially now&#8212;<br>and what would I tell?</p><p>Mes jours aussi d&#233;clinent ;<br>les r&#233;seaux sociaux entrent dans leur cr&#233;puscule.<br>Pourquoi rassembler quoi que ce soit,<br>tout sp&#233;cialement maintenant &#8212;<br>et qu&#8217;aurais-je &#224; raconter ?</p><div><hr></div><h3>06</h3><p><strong>&#25991;&#23383;&#38754;&#12391;&#20998;&#12363;&#12427;&#12363;&#12366;&#12426;&#12398;&#12356;&#12414;&#12424;&#12354;&#12426;<br>&#12371;&#12392;&#12400;&#12398;&#21521;&#12371;&#12358;&#12394;&#12425;&#12373;&#12427;&#12363;&#12425;&#12384;</strong></p><p>There is a present<br>we know only from the face of words.<br>Beyond language, though,<br>there remains<br>this unaccustomed body.</p><p>Il existe un pr&#233;sent<br>que nous ne connaissons que par la face des mots.<br>Mais au-del&#224; du langage<br>demeure encore<br>ce corps qui ne s&#8217;y habitue pas.</p><div><hr></div><h3>07</h3><p><strong>&#36933;&#24310;&#12377;&#12427;&#12402;&#12392;&#12398;&#12415;TREK<br>&#19968;&#21608;&#22238;&#20108;&#21608;&#22238;&#12363;&#12425;&#19977;&#21608;&#22806;&#12408;</strong></p><p>Only humans lag behind&#8212;TREK:<br>one orbit,<br>then two,<br>and from the third<br>out beyond the rounds.</p><p>Seuls les humains demeurent en retard &#8212; TREK :<br>un tour,<br>puis deux,<br>et au troisi&#232;me<br>hors de l&#8217;orbite.</p><div><hr></div><h3>08</h3><p><strong>&#12356;&#12365;&#36949;&#12358;&#21521;&#12365;&#12364;&#27671;&#12395;&#12394;&#12426;&#12512;&#12461;&#12395;&#12394;&#12426;<br>&#36899;&#25237;&#36899;&#37782;&#38706;&#20986;&#12496;&#12452;&#12450;&#12473;</strong></p><p>Directions cross and miss;<br>we mind the difference,<br>then lose our minds&#8212;<br>post after post, chain after chain,<br>the bias of exposure.</p><p>Les directions se croisent et se manquent ;<br>la diff&#233;rence nous travaille,<br>puis nous nous braquons &#8212;<br>publication apr&#232;s publication, cha&#238;ne apr&#232;s cha&#238;ne,<br>le biais de l&#8217;exposition.</p><div><hr></div><h3>09</h3><p><strong>&#22833;&#25943;&#12434;&#35377;&#12373;&#12396;&#23376;&#32946;&#12390;&#22833;&#25943;&#12377;<br>&#33073;&#32218;&#33258;&#24049;&#20013;&#12524;&#12540;&#12523;&#12394;&#12365;&#30165;</strong></p><p>Raise a child allowing no failure,<br>and parenting fails.<br>Derailment, self-centered&#8212;<br>yet what remains<br>is a trace without rails.</p><p>&#201;lever un enfant sans permettre l&#8217;&#233;chec,<br>et l&#8217;&#233;ducation &#233;choue.<br>D&#233;raillement, &#233;gocentrisme &#8212;<br>pourtant ce qui reste<br>est une trace sans rails.</p><div><hr></div><h3>10</h3><p><strong>&#35609;&#12426;&#34394;&#12429;&#12405;&#21322;&#29983;&#12394;&#12365;&#31505;&#12356;<br>&#20605;&#12426;&#12390;&#12418;&#36066;&#12434;&#23398;&#12400;&#12435;&#12434;</strong></p><p>Humility turns hollow&#8212;<br>half a life, no reflection,<br>a laugh almost weeping.<br>Even in pretense,<br>learn from the wise.</p><p>L&#8217;humilit&#233; se creuse &#8212;<br>une demi-vie sans r&#233;flexion,<br>un rire presque en larmes.<br>M&#234;me dans le semblant,<br>apprenons des sages.</p><div><hr></div><h3>11</h3><p><strong>&#38560;&#12428;&#12383;&#12427;&#30495;&#23455;&#25968;&#22810;&#12394;&#12356;&#12414;&#12424;&#12434;<br>&#12394;&#12382;&#12426;&#12383;&#12435;&#12363;&#12399;&#12394;&#12382;&#12426;&#12390;&#35598;&#12427;</strong></p><p>Countless truths lie hidden<br>in this present age.<br>A tracing tanka?<br>Trace them&#8212;<br>and mystery begins again.</p><p>D&#8217;innombrables v&#233;rit&#233;s se cachent<br>dans notre pr&#233;sent.<br>Un tanka qui les trace ?<br>Trace-les &#8212;<br>et l&#8217;&#233;nigme recommence.</p><div><hr></div><h3>12</h3><p><strong>&#12522;&#12501;&#12524;&#12452;&#12531;&#30406;&#36362;&#12426;&#12495;&#12524;&#20316;&#27861;&#12398;&#12465;<br>&#21644;&#27671;&#12354;&#12358;&#12369;&#12364;&#12428;&#38706;&#22825;&#12398;&#12420;&#12368;&#12425;</strong></p><p>Refrain&#8212;Bon dance:<br>the everyday art of festival,<br>spirits mingling,<br>impurity opening into air<br>around the outdoor tower.</p><p>Refrain &#8212; danse de Bon :<br>l&#8217;art quotidien de la f&#234;te,<br>les souffles se m&#234;lent,<br>l&#8217;impur s&#8217;ouvre &#224; l&#8217;air<br>autour de la tour sous le ciel.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Tracing into Mystery</h2><p>To trace is not merely to copy.</p><p>One traces a road.<br>One traces the wise.<br>One traces words, customs, errors, bodies, and the steps of a dance.</p><p>And in tracing, the tracer changes.</p><p>A trace followed becomes another trace.<br>A road traveled does not necessarily become a rail.<br>Repetition does not necessarily return us to the same place.</p><p>Perhaps this is why mystery remains.</p><p>We trace what has already been left behind,<br>and something that had been hidden begins to appear.</p><p>Yet what appears does not close the question.</p><p><strong>We trace.<br>We change.<br>We encounter again.<br>We enter mystery.</strong></p><div><hr></div><h2>Tracer jusqu&#8217;&#224; l&#8217;&#233;nigme</h2><p>Tracer, ce n&#8217;est pas simplement copier.</p><p>On suit une route.<br>On suit les sages.<br>On retrace des mots, des coutumes, des erreurs, des corps et les pas d&#8217;une danse.</p><p>Et en tra&#231;ant, celui qui trace se transforme.</p><p>Une trace suivie devient une autre trace.<br>Une route parcourue ne devient pas n&#233;cessairement un rail.<br>La r&#233;p&#233;tition ne nous ram&#232;ne pas n&#233;cessairement au m&#234;me endroit.</p><p>C&#8217;est peut-&#234;tre pour cela que l&#8217;&#233;nigme demeure.</p><p>Nous suivons ce qui a d&#233;j&#224; laiss&#233; sa trace,<br>et quelque chose qui &#233;tait cach&#233; commence &#224; appara&#238;tre.</p><p>Mais ce qui appara&#238;t ne cl&#244;t pas la question.</p><p><strong>Nous tra&#231;ons.<br>Nous changeons.<br>Nous rencontrons &#224; nouveau.<br>Nous entrons dans l&#8217;&#233;nigme.</strong></p><div><hr></div><p><strong>Inter-Phase Co-Editing</strong><br><em>A poem is not translated. It continues becoming across phases.</em><br><em>Rewritten across languages, intelligences, and time.</em></p><p><strong>&#20908;&#26408; &#19968;&#29380;&#65372;Fuyuki Itteki</strong><br><em>&#28216;&#35424;&#36655; &#8212; Selected Tanka, Fifth Collection</em></p><div><hr></div><p style="text-align: right;"><em>&#169; K.E. Itekki 2026</em></p><div><hr></div><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://campus6214.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&#30331;&#37682;&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;ja&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Camp@Us &#12399;&#35501;&#32773;&#12398;&#25903;&#25588;&#12395;&#12424;&#12387;&#12390;&#25104;&#12426;&#31435;&#12387;&#12390;&#12356;&#12414;&#12377;&#12290;&#26032;&#12375;&#12356;&#12509;&#12473;&#12488;&#12434;&#21463;&#12369;&#21462;&#12426;&#12289;&#31169;&#12398;&#27963;&#21205;&#12434;&#24540;&#25588;&#12375;&#12390;&#12356;&#12383;&#12384;&#12367;&#12395;&#12399;&#12289;&#28961;&#26009;&#12414;&#12383;&#12399;&#26377;&#26009;&#12398;&#36092;&#35501;&#32773;&#12395;&#12394;&#12427;&#12371;&#12392;&#12434;&#12372;&#26908;&#35342;&#12367;&#12384;&#12373;&#12356;&#12290;</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="&#12513;&#12540;&#12523;&#12450;&#12489;&#12524;&#12473;&#12434;&#20837;&#21147;&#12375;&#12390;&#12367;&#12384;&#12373;&#12356;&#8230;" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="&#30331;&#37682;"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><p style="text-align: right;"></p> ]]>
